e this  idea that when you go to Europe you're  gonna have this like fantasy eat Pray  Love experience right and it was just  totally nothing that I had imagined it  was even better at the any you you were  actually serving some of your  grandmother's  peas correct yeah we're actually both my  grandmother's so there's a little bit of  like a Jewish influence and I'm  Hungarian influence so we're doing a  schnitzel makes it onto the menu or Ron  tutush as you would call it a Nigerian  stuffed cabbage although it's not a pork  stuffed cabbage it is a it's my version  of it I love that you said that you you  you want to preserve your grandmother's  Hungary mm-hmm there's not a lot of  there's not many Hungarians like my  grandmother left and I want to preserve  her cooking but in a new way and that's  the best way to do it kind of introduce  it to everyone and as you are we  introduced the dish to you and you sign  it who would you have this meal I would  have this meal with my Hungarian  grandfather who unfortunately passed  away when I was much younger so he's the  only immediate family member that I  never had the opportunity to cook for  probably would want to share this with  him oh that's wonderful  well chef Jeremy we so appreciate you  being here and thank you  and I always like to show the dish Matt  Mayes that's a nice one very much it is  and for more on Chef Jeremy and the dish  head to our website at  cBS This Morning Calm

